From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8010-7: Give the iPhone 7 charger the USB
 host's grant

The iPhone 7 and 7 Plus have the same SN2400 charger and charging policy
as the A9 iPhones: the input foldback ramps towards the 2 A input limit
until VBUS droops, so on a computer port nothing caps it at what the host
allows. Give usbdev usb-psy-name, as s800x-iphone.dtsi does, so the
charger follows the host's grant and a wall adapter (a suspended,
unconfigured port) keeps the foldback.

The A9 iPhone change was measured on the iPhone 6s Plus (500 mA from a
Mac port). Untested on the iPhone 7.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi
index 7373105..ac86a47 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-7.dtsi
@@ -280,3 +280,8 @@
 &touchclk {
 	clock-frequency = <32768>;
 };
+
+/* The USB device controller tells the SN2400 driver what the USB host allows. */
+&usbdev {
+	usb-psy-name = "usb";
+};
